# garbage stuff in root dir
*.txt*
# The AXP1-ZnQ (Architect's eXecution Protocol 1) address catalog
# (night-learning-into-darkness-1): the repos-for-ci family files are
# tracked on purpose - the tested address pool the failover resolver
# reads and the Sunday maintenance pass rewrites. Same estate law as
# the pinned fingerprint re-include below.
!repos-for-ci/*.txt
# The D5 pinned fingerprint is a tracked trust anchor (night-netrunner-Z1):
# the wall above would swallow it and break build/gpg.rs's include_str! —
# re-include it explicitly (the zelynic estate law).
!assets/gpg/pinned-maintainer-fpr.txt
# The proptest regression stores (night-netrunner-Z2, the zelynic
# proof-layer shape): tracked ledgers of every counterexample the
# property lanes have caught and shrunk — committed on purpose so
# every contributor and CI lane replays the exact witnesses.
!test/tests/property-regressions.txt
!test/cosmic_dragon_incubator/tests/emission_conformance-regressions.txt
*.ruff*
.vs/

# Bot dependency-update staging (night-zen-1 hotfix: download-artifact
# staging must live under runner.temp, never in the work tree)
.auto-update/


# night-cafe-1 (the zelynic raw-binary law): a raw compiled binary is a
# local build/extract product, never tracked. The tracked lane for a
# vendored verification package is the .gz package with its .b3sum
# sidecar (docs/VERIFY_RELEASE.md section 5). The fuzz seed fixtures
# under fuzz/seeds/ are 5-10 byte escape-sequence test data consumed by
# the validator tests - tracked on purpose.
/cosmostrix
/scripts/labs-exp/cosmostrix-*
!scripts/labs-exp/cosmostrix-*.gz
!scripts/labs-exp/cosmostrix-*.b3sum
